# Code ownership for runlog-vocabularies.
#
# Vocabulary data is consumed by both the runlog server (sanitizer) and the
# verifier (pre-sign check) — a malicious or careless edit here would
# weaken the default-deny gate for every Runlog submission. So every change
# to allow-list data, the scope registry, or the validator gets owner
# review before merge. The catch-all `*` rule covers anything not matched
# by a more specific pattern (workflows, README, LICENSE, scripts).

*                                          @l4ci
domains/                                   @l4ci
protocols/                                 @l4ci
scope-registry.yaml                        @l4ci
scripts/validate_vocabularies.py           @l4ci
.github/workflows/                         @l4ci
